# Line endings. gate-line-endings (.github/workflows/gate-line-endings.yml) HARD FAILS
# a PR whose changed files are stored with CRLF. Without an attribute covering the
# path, git happily re-offers CRLF on the very next edit, so the same PR gets blocked
# again -- that recurrence is precisely why the gate exists rather than relying on
# .gitattributes alone. This repo's entire CRLF backlog is Python, so cover *.py.
#
# This does NOT rewrite existing blobs; it only takes effect the next time a file is
# staged. 20 pre-existing CRLF .py files under services/orchestrator/ remain and are
# reported as warnings on pushes to main. Clean them with:
#   git add --renormalize . && git commit -m "chore: normalise line endings to LF"
# (deliberately not done here -- it would bury this security fix under ~20k
# whitespace-only diff lines and collide with the PRs currently in flight).
*.py text eol=lf
